1
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,359
You can't risk my mom's life over your mindset.

2
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,079
I don't understand what you're saying.

3
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,120
I just won't agree to it.

4
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,120
I'm her daughter.

5
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,599
I can take responsibility for my decision.

6
00:01:46,599 --> 00:01:47,280
Can you?

7
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,519
I am her husband.

8
00:01:49,599 --> 00:01:50,840
And I'm still your father.

9
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:01,599
The phone.

10
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,519
The surgery must be done.

11
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:10,919
What does she mean?

12
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:11,960
Dad.

13
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,000
What do you mean?

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,280
What "must be done"?

15
00:02:14,879 --> 00:02:16,639
Not unless I'm the one in the hospital bed,

16
00:02:16,639 --> 00:02:18,199
waiting for you to sign the papers.

17
00:02:42,439 --> 00:02:43,080
What happened?

18
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:43,879
Why are you in such a rush?

19
00:02:45,159 --> 00:02:46,840
My grandfather had a stroke back then.

20
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,919
The villagers got medicine for him,

21
00:02:49,199 --> 00:02:50,039
but couldn't save him.

22
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:52,479
It was because his treatment was delayed.

23
00:02:53,639 --> 00:02:55,759
Your mother just fell ill.

24
00:02:55,919 --> 00:02:57,039
There's definitely still time.

25
00:02:57,039 --> 00:02:58,439
Lingzhi is listed in here.

26
00:02:58,560 --> 00:02:59,560
It's the guiding herb.

27
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,919
We can't do without it.

28
00:03:00,919 --> 00:03:02,560
I grew up in the mountains.

29
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:03,919
I know how to find it.

30
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:11,280
Right.

31
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:14,840
I also have an old prescription here.

32
00:03:15,039 --> 00:03:18,000
Try to get as many of the herbs as you can.

33
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Even if you can't find them all, it's fine.

34
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,800
We finally convinced your father.

35
00:03:28,199 --> 00:03:29,360
The surgery will be scheduled as soon as possible.

36
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:30,599
Don't worry.

37
00:03:59,759 --> 00:04:00,520
What's this?

38
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,680
I found this in Lin Kanshan's

39
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,159
desk.

40
00:04:04,639 --> 00:04:06,080
On the day he came to the mainland,

41
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,120
he brought this old newspaper from the airport.

42
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,439
It has dates and news,

43
00:04:10,439 --> 00:04:12,159
and numbers in the articles.

44
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,639
I didn't know if it'd be useful,

45
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,040
so I copied them down for you.

46
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:54,839
Right, right, right.

47
00:04:54,959 --> 00:04:56,279
I'm here, I'm here.

48
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:58,879
The new shop is being renovated.

49
00:04:58,879 --> 00:05:00,360
Once it's done, I'll call you all back.

50
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,519
Don't worry, don't worry.

51
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:03,800
Goodbye, Sister Xia.

52
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:04,439
I'll miss you.

53
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,959
Sister Xia, I'll miss you so much.

54
00:05:06,519 --> 00:05:07,160
It's fine.

55
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,399
With me around, would I ever shortchange you?

56
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:09,839
Here.

57
00:05:10,279 --> 00:05:11,279
Thank you, Sister Xia.

58
00:05:11,279 --> 00:05:11,959
Boss, Boss!

59
00:05:11,959 --> 00:05:13,439
Sister Xia, Sister Xia!

60
00:05:13,639 --> 00:05:15,000
I have elderly parents and kids to feed.

61
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,120
I can barely put food on the table!

62
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:17,959
Hold on, hold on.

63
00:05:17,959 --> 00:05:19,639
Let's get in line first, alright?

64
00:05:19,639 --> 00:05:21,480
Line up first, everyone.

65
00:05:22,079 --> 00:05:22,920
Come on, guys!

66
00:05:23,279 --> 00:05:25,519
If you don't line up, how can I pay you?

67
00:05:25,519 --> 00:05:27,079
We've known each other for so long.

68
00:05:27,079 --> 00:05:27,600
All these years.

69
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,519
Don't you trust what kind of person I am?

70
00:05:29,519 --> 00:05:30,560
We trust you, of course we do.

71
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,920
The money is all right here.

72
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,800
Let's form a proper line.

73
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,120
I'll pay every single one of you today.

74
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,480
If you don't get paid, hold me accountable.

75
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,160
Everyone will get paid.

76
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,519
Everyone will get paid, don't worry.

77
00:05:38,519 --> 00:05:39,079
You'll get it.

78
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,639
You will, that's a promise.

79
00:05:40,639 --> 00:05:41,839
If you don't, come hold me to it.

80
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:42,839
All right, all right.

81
00:05:43,199 --> 00:05:43,800
Thank you for understanding.

82
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,920
Thanks for understanding!

83
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,959
You're all here to collect your pay.

84
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:48,120
Right? I totally understand.

85
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:48,920
Sister Xia.

86
00:05:49,639 --> 00:05:50,600
Look for that name.

87
00:05:50,879 --> 00:05:52,120
When are you reopening?

88
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:52,800
Renovations are underway.

89
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,800
We'll reopen as soon as they're done.

90
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:56,319
I'm right here, don't worry.

91
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:57,000
Sister Xia.

92
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:57,800
Right.

93
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,439
Where's Boss Wen?

94
00:05:59,120 --> 00:05:59,720
Boss Wen?

95
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:00,560
Next door, he's next door!

96
00:06:01,079 --> 00:06:01,680
Yes, right over there.

97
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,560
Girl, let me go first.

98
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,399
I've got you covered.

99
00:06:03,399 --> 00:06:05,120
Don't worry, come find me anytime.

100
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:06,600
Just come to me.

101
00:06:19,199 --> 00:06:20,519
Didn't you go to Macau, China?

102
00:06:23,839 --> 00:06:25,480
I called non-stop and you never picked up.

103
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,079
Afraid I'd cling to you?

104
00:06:31,279 --> 00:06:32,120
I'm pregnant.

105
00:06:35,279 --> 00:06:35,839
It's yours.

106
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:41,680
I'm pretty surprised.

107
00:06:42,839 --> 00:06:44,600
That I've still got it in me.

108
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,199
I wanted to tell you ages ago,

109
00:06:47,399 --> 00:06:48,279
but I couldn't reach you anywhere.

110
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,040
I had someone check.

111
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,279
It's a boy.

112
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,279
Why didn't you say so earlier?

113
00:07:01,439 --> 00:07:02,600
Doesn't the smoke bother you?

114
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,120
No way, it's full of smoke in here.

115
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,120
Go inside, go inside, go on.

116
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,519
Let's stop testing for today.

117
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,240
Get some rest early.

118
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,319
Don't ruin your health,

119
00:08:01,319 --> 00:08:02,720
or you'll have nothing left.

120
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:08,199
When we get old,

121
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:10,680
if one of us ends up in the hospital

122
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,839
waiting for surgery,

123
00:08:12,279 --> 00:08:13,759
the other will need to make the call

124
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,319
and lend a hand.

125
00:08:21,279 --> 00:08:22,360
You go to sleep first.

126
00:08:22,959 --> 00:08:24,000
I'll try one last set.

127
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:29,000
Then wake me up early to take over.

128
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:46,759
What's wrong?

129
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:56,840
The front-page newspaper headline,

130
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:58,399
taking the initials of each first word,

131
00:09:58,399 --> 00:10:00,840
plus the digits of his arrival date,

132
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,720
that's his base cipher.

133
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:05,919
We're stuck.

134
00:10:40,519 --> 00:10:42,639
With so many passwords to guess,

135
00:10:42,919 --> 00:10:45,440
it'll take us until 2026!

136
00:10:46,519 --> 00:10:47,960
The base digits are already cracked.

137
00:10:48,519 --> 00:10:50,159
Most of the passwords are the same.

138
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:52,039
You can't remember them, and neither can he.

139
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,000
So as long as the base digits stay the same,

140
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,440
we only have to guess the remaining digits.

141
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:56,919
Give one a try.

142
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,360
Attention.

143
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,480
Two of you are being released today.

144
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,080
Jin Chizhong, wait a moment.

145
00:12:10,279 --> 00:12:11,559
Cao Liaoping, get ready first.

146
00:12:11,679 --> 00:12:12,360
In five minutes,

147
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,759
someone will take you to the registration office.

148
00:12:14,399 --> 00:12:15,080
Dismissed.

149
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,279
Congratulations, Brother Cao.

150
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,200
Cheers.

151
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,879
Congratulations on your fresh start.

152
00:13:17,519 --> 00:13:18,320
Thank you.

153
00:13:25,159 --> 00:13:27,039
It's been years since I had such a feast.

154
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,799
Went in back in '96,

155
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,720
got out in '09.

156
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:34,240
Thirteen years.

157
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:37,080
Thirteen years without seeing

158
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,919
this much delicious food.

159
00:13:42,159 --> 00:13:43,559
What are your plans from now on?

160
00:13:44,159 --> 00:13:45,919
Just take it one step at a time.

161
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,080
In 1995, you went to Beijing.

162
00:13:51,679 --> 00:13:53,240
Using the money from Taiwan, China,

163
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,519
you bought an apartment in Chaoyang.

164
00:13:56,759 --> 00:13:58,200
It was put under Cao Xiao'ou's name.

165
00:13:58,679 --> 00:14:00,360
Do you know how much it's worth now?

166
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:02,559
It went up tenfold.

167
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:05,159
Can you believe that?

168
00:14:08,279 --> 00:14:09,000
Of course.

169
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,279
It's now considered confiscated assets.

170
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,279
As for this key...

171
00:14:13,279 --> 00:14:15,080
whether it ever returns to your hands

172
00:14:15,759 --> 00:14:17,440
depends entirely on your performance.

173
00:14:18,279 --> 00:14:19,879
Earning redemption through merit, to me,

174
00:14:19,879 --> 00:14:21,519
has never been an empty slogan.

175
00:14:22,799 --> 00:14:26,000
Remember that old classmate of yours?

176
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,480
Everyone's here!

177
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,600
Hey there, Old Zhang.

178
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:32,159
You're all here.

179
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:34,840
You're here so early, Mr. Zhao.

180
00:14:39,919 --> 00:14:41,879
Little Cao got here even earlier.

181
00:14:41,879 --> 00:14:43,000
What about Little Jia?

182
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,399
Why hasn't he arrived yet?

183
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,960
We're all here.

184
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:47,360
Is he outside smoking?

185
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,320
Which Little Jia?

186
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:50,200
Mr. Zhao's prized top rivals.

187
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:53,600
One ranked first in the school,

188
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:56,320
the other ranked second.

189
00:14:57,559 --> 00:14:59,159
Speak of Cao Cao, and here he comes.

190
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,360
Jia Chunlin!

191
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,200
Jia Chunlin!

192
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,240
Mr. Zhao was just talking about you.

193
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,720
Engineer Jia.

194
00:15:05,639 --> 00:15:06,919
Sorry, my apologies.

195
00:15:06,919 --> 00:15:07,600
Engineer Jia.

196
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,480
Don't shoot, don't shoot!

197
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:09,480
Take photos of the older folks.

198
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,039
Long time no see!

199
00:15:14,039 --> 00:15:15,519
Old Cao!

200
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,399
When did you get out?

201
00:15:21,399 --> 00:15:22,480
You got released

202
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,399
and didn't even let me know?

203
00:15:24,399 --> 00:15:26,440
I should've thrown a welcome dinner

204
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:27,720
and treated you to drinks!

205
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:28,879
Are you serious?

206
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:31,000
Your favorite red wine...

207
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,600
It's stored at my place right now.

208
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:33,960
I bought it long ago,

209
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,000
kept it stored all this time,

210
00:15:35,399 --> 00:15:36,799
until it's properly aged.

211
00:15:37,679 --> 00:15:40,080
These past ten-odd years went by so fast.

212
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Tell you what, you pick the place,

213
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:43,759
and I'll pick the time.

214
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,000
The two of us have to drink that wine.

215
00:15:47,759 --> 00:15:48,840
No day like today.

216
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,240
Why not make it today?

217
00:15:50,519 --> 00:15:52,039
Today really won't work.

218
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,480
After this wraps up,

219
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:54,639
I have another meeting.

220
00:15:54,639 --> 00:15:56,440
Another day, another day.

221
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,559
Absolutely.

222
00:15:58,519 --> 00:15:59,480
Jia Chunlin.

223
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:01,000
You make sure to remind me.

224
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:04,519
Mr. Zhao, please don't get up!

225
00:16:04,519 --> 00:16:06,840
Students shouldn't make teachers stand.

226
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,159
Have you been here long?

227
00:16:08,159 --> 00:16:10,480
Back then, you punished me by making me copy homework,

228
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:12,519
and I ended up the top Gaokao scorer!

229
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,480
You were smart.

230
00:16:14,879 --> 00:16:16,919
It was all thanks to your own hard work.

231
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:19,039
Come on, everyone squeeze in closer!

232
00:16:19,039 --> 00:16:19,919
Move closer together.

233
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:22,360
Switch spots, switch spots.

234
00:16:26,279 --> 00:16:27,559
You stepped on my shoe.

235
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:28,000
Sorry, I'm so sorry.

236
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,240
So clumsy.

237
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:31,000
Didn't see it, my bad.

238
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:34,759
Little Cao.

239
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:36,480
Still as annoying as ever.

240
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,480
Pretty expensive shoes, huh?

241
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,679
Italian pigskin, handmade.

242
00:16:44,679 --> 00:16:45,919
How much did they cost?

243
00:16:46,879 --> 00:16:48,399
That stuff of yours...

244
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,240
How much will Taiwan, China pay for it?

245
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:55,320
Let's team up—make more and spend less.

246
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:56,639
Gotten brave, haven't you?

247
00:16:56,639 --> 00:16:57,840
You want to go back to prison?

248
00:16:58,240 --> 00:16:59,399
Aren't you afraid I'll report you?

249
00:17:09,279 --> 00:17:11,000
Something you went through hell to get

250
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,240
should be sold at a high price.

251
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,519
One copy isn't enough.

252
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,200
If I were you, I'd sell two.

253
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,880
Everything is digital nowadays.

254
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,519
No more film rolls.

255
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:25,279
What are you storing it on?

256
00:17:26,279 --> 00:17:29,119
A USB drive or email?

257
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,279
Everyone, say it with me!

258
00:17:33,359 --> 00:17:35,279
Cheese!

259
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,799
For people from our parts,

260
00:17:36,799 --> 00:17:39,559
starting with a cup of tea is the rule.

261
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:43,880
I'm happy. Truly thrilled today.

262
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:46,680
Liaoping is finally out.

263
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:52,039
See? Feels familiar, right?

264
00:17:54,799 --> 00:17:56,599
Classmates for three years in high school.

265
00:17:56,599 --> 00:17:59,440
As our homeroom teacher said, it's fate.

266
00:18:00,039 --> 00:18:03,680
Today is our 40th high school reunion.

267
00:18:04,519 --> 00:18:06,160
Liaoping...

268
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:10,279
How many 40-year spans do we get in life?

269
00:18:10,279 --> 00:18:11,440
Look at the bond between us.

270
00:18:11,759 --> 00:18:12,960
Same high school,

271
00:18:13,279 --> 00:18:14,680
same college,

272
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,200
and the same workplace.

273
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,680
You survived a major ordeal,

274
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,480
and I'm here to throw you a welcome dinner,

275
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:22,200
truly happy for you,

276
00:18:23,839 --> 00:18:24,759
so happy for you.

277
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:25,720
Come on.

278
00:18:27,359 --> 00:18:30,039
If this isn't fate, what is?

279
00:18:31,519 --> 00:18:32,319
To fate.

280
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,680
To fate.

281
00:18:35,599 --> 00:18:37,400
Remember that year we went to Beijing?

282
00:18:37,839 --> 00:18:39,359
We both drank way too much.

283
00:18:39,359 --> 00:18:40,880
I thought to myself back then,

284
00:18:41,119 --> 00:18:42,720
you, Cao Liaoping—

285
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:44,160
as if I didn't know you.

286
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,359
You little bourgeois,

287
00:18:46,359 --> 00:18:48,079
you only liked drinking red wine.

288
00:18:48,079 --> 00:18:49,839
Who would've thought?

289
00:18:49,839 --> 00:18:53,079
You'd chug Erguotou so ruthlessly too.

290
00:18:53,079 --> 00:18:53,880
Aren't you tired?

291
00:18:55,799 --> 00:18:56,599
What?

292
00:18:56,599 --> 00:18:57,599
I asked, aren't you tired?

293
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:01,279
Like at school parties back then,

294
00:19:01,279 --> 00:19:03,279
you did stand-up comedy on stage,

295
00:19:03,279 --> 00:19:04,799
and not a single classmate laughed.

296
00:19:05,119 --> 00:19:06,480
Don't you feel exhausted?

297
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,319
I just lacked the artistic talent.

298
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,160
Today, you're finally out.

299
00:19:17,559 --> 00:19:19,799
I'm happy. Truly thrilled.

300
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,519
The last time we were here,

301
00:19:21,839 --> 00:19:23,440
you asked if I had ever done

302
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:24,960
anything to betray our country.

303
00:19:25,599 --> 00:19:25,759
Let's not bring that up.

304
00:19:25,759 --> 00:19:27,680
I said I could swear an oath,

305
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,359
but the truth is, I lied.

306
00:19:30,359 --> 00:19:31,920
For all my bluster,

307
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,240
I was terrified on the inside.

308
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,519
Just like you are right now.

309
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,480
Food this good...

310
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:48,400
Dig in.

311
00:19:49,039 --> 00:19:51,319
When I was inside, I told them

312
00:19:52,039 --> 00:19:54,119
that once I was out, I'd eat lobster every day,

313
00:19:54,119 --> 00:19:55,200
until I threw up.

314
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:59,359
Until just the sight of it made me sick.

315
00:20:00,119 --> 00:20:00,920
But you know what?

316
00:20:01,319 --> 00:20:04,079
You never get sick of the good stuff.

317
00:20:05,279 --> 00:20:06,079
Eat.

318
00:20:09,759 --> 00:20:10,720
What do you want?

319
00:20:15,359 --> 00:20:17,119
Society is a university.

320
00:20:17,559 --> 00:20:18,920
And its current president

321
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,960
is named Ma Qi.

322
00:20:21,359 --> 00:20:22,160
You and I...

323
00:20:22,599 --> 00:20:24,799
could still be classmates.

324
00:20:26,839 --> 00:20:28,240
Brilliant.

325
00:20:31,119 --> 00:20:31,920
Forget "classmates."

326
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,319
From now on, you two are my bosses.

327
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:39,200
I'll do whatever you say.

328
00:20:42,839 --> 00:20:44,079
Here's to a great partnership.

329
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:57,000
Clean this place up tomorrow.

330
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,319
Once Old Cao gets back,

331
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:03,079
you'll be working here from now on.

332
00:22:04,799 --> 00:22:06,160
You can't smoke in here.

333
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:13,880
What are you laughing at?

334
00:22:46,759 --> 00:22:47,680
Brother Qi,

335
00:22:49,279 --> 00:22:50,200
a toast to you.

336
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:03,759
Since ancient times,

337
00:23:04,759 --> 00:23:06,400
both at home and abroad,

338
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:09,000
intelligence work has always been about people.

339
00:23:09,519 --> 00:23:11,680
With people, info flows from all sides.

340
00:23:12,119 --> 00:23:13,880
Your funding has to go to someone anyway.

341
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:16,880
We just want to earn it.

342
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,119
I wouldn't dare lie to you.

343
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:22,880
Of all lines of work, this is the only thing I can do.

344
00:23:23,279 --> 00:23:24,880
And deep down, I genuinely love it.

345
00:23:25,319 --> 00:23:27,160
Back then, I just wanted to do the work.

346
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:28,640
Now, all I care about is making money.

347
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:30,759
My health hasn't been good these past two years.

348
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:33,319
I have to plan for my old age.

349
00:23:34,119 --> 00:23:34,920
Brother Qi.

350
00:23:36,279 --> 00:23:36,839
I believe that when it comes to

351
00:23:36,839 --> 00:23:39,119
collecting and analyzing intelligence,

352
00:23:39,119 --> 00:23:41,039
I have a certain talent and instinct.

353
00:23:41,039 --> 00:23:42,279
I don't need much insider info.

354
00:23:42,839 --> 00:23:43,440
Just by relying on

355
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:45,160
open news on TV and in newspapers,

356
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:46,279
and with a little study,

357
00:23:46,279 --> 00:23:48,680
I can grasp a lot of hidden information.

358
00:23:49,039 --> 00:23:50,400
The key to intelligence work

359
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:52,680
is spotting details and patterns in the news.

360
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:56,119
It's like picking a lock—once the key fits,

361
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,799
every door opens wide.

362
00:23:59,119 --> 00:24:00,119
Humble as I am,

363
00:24:00,119 --> 00:24:01,759
I just enjoy reading the news and papers,

364
00:24:01,759 --> 00:24:02,960
analyzing every little detail.

365
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:05,000
Political trends and stock market trends

366
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:05,880
operate on the exact same logic.

367
00:24:06,119 --> 00:24:07,279
No matter how many smokescreens are deployed,

368
00:24:07,599 --> 00:24:09,680
there is always an underlying logic.

369
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:10,319
As long as you put yourself

370
00:24:10,319 --> 00:24:11,799
in the shoes of the target,

371
00:24:11,799 --> 00:24:12,880
and see things from their perspective,

372
00:24:13,599 --> 00:24:15,240
even if a matter seems settled,

373
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:17,079
I can still deduce

374
00:24:17,079 --> 00:24:19,000
the root causes of the outcome and its trajectory.

375
00:24:21,839 --> 00:24:23,119
And once deduced,

376
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:26,880
every single piece is top-secret intelligence.

377
00:24:31,839 --> 00:24:34,240
Brother Qi, if I'm not mistaken,

378
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:38,519
you're casting a wide net across the Taiwan Strait, right?

379
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:41,960
I'm willing to be one of your meshes.

380
00:24:42,839 --> 00:24:44,079
And the more meshes you have,

381
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:45,920
the better it is, isn't it?

382
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:49,599
According to you,

383
00:24:49,839 --> 00:24:51,640
you're best at predictive analysis.

384
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:54,640
There are many elections going on out there lately.

385
00:24:55,359 --> 00:24:56,119
Tell me,

386
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,599
which winners can you predict?

387
00:25:00,599 --> 00:25:02,400
The European Parliament elections,

388
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:04,319
Taiwan, China's "three-in-one" elections,

389
00:25:04,319 --> 00:25:06,519
the Afghan presidential or Japanese prime minister elections...

390
00:25:07,079 --> 00:25:07,920
Take your pick.

391
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,240
Since it's right next door,

392
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:17,119
let's bet on Taiwan, China.

393
00:25:19,759 --> 00:25:20,519
Recently,

394
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:22,000
Taiwan, China's magistrate, mayoral,

395
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,039
councilor, and township mayoral races—

396
00:25:24,039 --> 00:25:25,799
the "three-in-one" elections were held.

397
00:25:25,799 --> 00:25:27,000
This is the Kuomintang's

398
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:28,599
first crucial electoral battle

399
00:25:28,759 --> 00:25:30,759
since returning to power last year.

400
00:25:30,759 --> 00:25:33,039
In the highly watched magistrate and mayoral race,

401
00:25:33,039 --> 00:25:35,640
per Taiwan, China's election authority,

402
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:37,160
the winners include:

403
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,640
Chang Tong-rong of Keelung City,

404
00:25:39,279 --> 00:25:41,000
Lin Tsung-hsien of Yilan County...

405
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:43,160
You really do know your stuff.

406
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:45,200
Cho Po-yuan of Changhua County,

407
00:25:45,599 --> 00:25:47,359
Lee Chao-ching of Nantou County,

408
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:49,519
Su Chih-fen of Yunlin County,

409
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:51,759
Tsao Chi-hung of Pingtung County,

410
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:53,880
Huang Chien-ting of Taitung County,

411
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:56,160
Fu Kun-chi of Hualien County,

412
00:25:56,759 --> 00:25:58,640
Wang Chien-fa of Penghu County,

413
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:00,559
Li Wo-shih of Kinmen County,

414
00:26:01,119 --> 00:26:02,880
and Yang Sui-sheng of Lienchiang County.

415
00:27:39,759 --> 00:27:42,359
How are things with Wen Zongshu lately?

416
00:27:43,319 --> 00:27:45,160
His bathhouse business hasn't picked up,

417
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,880
but he's been busy with the intel business.

418
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:48,440
Still, it's all right under our noses,

419
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:50,160
and fully under our control.

420
00:27:50,519 --> 00:27:51,920
Institute 761, Institute 762,

421
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,039
Xie Fengshi's workplace,

422
00:27:53,039 --> 00:27:54,839
and the locations that recently surfaced...

423
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:57,319
I think it's all part of Zhu Yingjia's game.

424
00:27:57,319 --> 00:27:59,400
His goal is to string these beads together

425
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:00,359
into a necklace.

426
00:28:00,759 --> 00:28:02,160
Fortunately, we responded quickly.

427
00:28:02,160 --> 00:28:03,319
Apart from the few beads

428
00:28:03,319 --> 00:28:04,799
Cao Liaoping managed to steal earlier,

429
00:28:04,799 --> 00:28:07,319
nothing else went as Zhu Yingjia wished.

430
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,839
If the day ever comes

431
00:28:12,279 --> 00:28:14,039
when Ma Qi sides with them,

432
00:28:14,039 --> 00:28:14,839
it'll be treason.

433
00:28:17,039 --> 00:28:17,960
What are you getting at?

434
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:22,400
If he gathers intel just for the money,

435
00:28:23,039 --> 00:28:24,559
why tip off Lin Kanshan?

436
00:28:25,039 --> 00:28:26,440
Out of brotherly loyalty?

437
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:28,720
I think he's waiting

438
00:28:28,720 --> 00:28:29,839
for the right opportunity

439
00:28:30,319 --> 00:28:31,680
to use as a bargaining chip

440
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:32,880
to cut a deal with Zhu Yingjia.

441
00:28:37,079 --> 00:28:38,319
He's far too ambitious.

442
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:40,359
I think he's completely out of control.

443
00:28:43,400 --> 00:28:45,559
Do you think someone as smart as him

444
00:28:46,359 --> 00:28:47,240
would defect to Taiwan, China?

445
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,599
The smarter a person is,

446
00:28:49,599 --> 00:28:50,599
the higher their IQ,

447
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:52,519
the bigger the mistakes they make.

448
00:29:32,519 --> 00:29:34,039
There was a lot I didn't believe before.

449
00:29:34,519 --> 00:29:36,039
Now that I'm older, I'm not in control.

450
00:29:36,680 --> 00:29:39,480
Lately, I keep having nightmares.

451
00:29:40,279 --> 00:29:41,119
And feeling anxious.

452
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:44,319
I knelt over there for a bit just now,

453
00:29:45,319 --> 00:29:46,519
and the panic went away immediately.

454
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:48,519
Isn't that amazing?

455
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:52,440
Did something happen?

456
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:54,599
Two of my friends passed away.

457
00:29:55,559 --> 00:29:56,720
They didn't go in peace.

458
00:29:58,079 --> 00:29:59,519
When we were young,

459
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,359
weren't we all wild and reckless?

460
00:30:01,359 --> 00:30:02,839
Afraid of nothing under the sun.

461
00:30:03,079 --> 00:30:04,000
As we get older,

462
00:30:04,319 --> 00:30:05,480
there's much more to revere.

463
00:30:05,839 --> 00:30:06,839
That's a good thing, too.

464
00:30:09,200 --> 00:30:11,599
Brother Qi, all these years,

465
00:30:14,359 --> 00:30:15,599
have you ever feared anything?

466
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:18,319
Of course.

467
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:20,119
Lately, I'm especially afraid of dying.

468
00:30:22,279 --> 00:30:24,880
Lying in a hospital bed, barely living,

469
00:30:25,480 --> 00:30:26,559
unable to live comfortably, yet unable to die.

470
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:30,039
I wonder what will become of us

471
00:30:30,039 --> 00:30:31,400
when we grow old.

472
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,240
Yet I dare not get my fortune told.

473
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:35,200
It's like watching a TV drama:

474
00:30:35,319 --> 00:30:37,920
you want to see the end, but dread it, too.

475
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,240
So you can only drift along in a daze.

476
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:43,599
Why are you so sentimental today?

477
00:30:44,559 --> 00:30:45,680
Thinking of writing poetry lately?

478
00:30:55,079 --> 00:30:56,799
Look at those who got caught.

479
00:30:56,799 --> 00:30:59,160
It's always been the same, throughout history.

480
00:30:59,319 --> 00:31:02,079
On the surface, it seems coincidental,

481
00:31:02,480 --> 00:31:04,119
but in truth, it was all fated.

482
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:08,480
We think we're making our own decisions,

483
00:31:09,359 --> 00:31:11,240
but Heaven already arranged it all.

484
00:31:16,559 --> 00:31:19,000
When did Mr. Zhu's mother pass away?

485
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:21,200
You're quite well-informed.

486
00:31:23,839 --> 00:31:25,000
Yesterday at one in the morning.

487
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:28,119
Pass along a message for me.

488
00:31:29,079 --> 00:31:30,160
I want to go there myself.

489
00:31:31,759 --> 00:31:32,559
To pay my respects in person.

490
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:40,039
Under the agreement between ARATS

491
00:31:40,039 --> 00:31:42,119
and the Straits Exchange Foundation at their third summit,

492
00:31:42,119 --> 00:31:44,519
the Cross-Strait Air Transport Agreement,

493
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:47,119
scheduled cross-strait maiden flights,

494
00:31:47,559 --> 00:31:48,680
marking cross-strait air transport's

495
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:50,799
entry into regular operations.

496
00:31:50,799 --> 00:31:52,319
Weekly round-trip flights

497
00:31:52,319 --> 00:31:53,039
Over here! Over here!

498
00:31:53,039 --> 00:31:54,480
will increase from the charter stage

499
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:57,640
of 108 flights to 270.

500
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:59,519
Since 2003,

501
00:31:59,519 --> 00:32:03,039
cross-strait aviation went from charters to direct flights,

502
00:32:03,319 --> 00:32:05,400
stops in Macau, China & Hong Kong, China

503
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:08,359
to just routing via Hong Kong, China's FIR

504
00:32:08,359 --> 00:32:10,880
achieving historic breakthroughs time and again.

505
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:30,359
How many days, how many years I've waited...

506
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:32,440
waited until my eyes nearly went blind.

507
00:32:33,279 --> 00:32:34,440
I was even afraid...

508
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:36,839
afraid I wouldn't see you before I retired.

509
00:32:39,279 --> 00:32:40,279
You've lost weight.

510
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:42,519
At least six to ten jin.

511
00:32:42,799 --> 00:32:44,880
My blood sugar is too high now.

512
00:32:45,119 --> 00:32:46,920
If I don't watch what I eat,

513
00:32:46,920 --> 00:32:48,160
they'll have to saw my leg off.

514
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:51,200
If I'd known this day would come,

515
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:52,839
back on that flight to Beijing,

516
00:32:52,839 --> 00:32:54,680
I wouldn't have feared your stare.

517
00:32:56,960 --> 00:32:59,200
Excuse me, could I borrow your newspaper?

518
00:33:01,359 --> 00:33:02,000
Here.

519
00:33:02,319 --> 00:33:03,119
Thanks.

520
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:05,000
There were none left when I tried to grab one.

521
00:33:05,720 --> 00:33:06,440
You're welcome.

522
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:08,680
You know what?

523
00:33:08,680 --> 00:33:10,400
One more second under that look,

524
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:12,079
and I would've pissed my pants.

525
00:33:13,839 --> 00:33:15,160
People say women have intuition,

526
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,160
but that was the first time I realized

527
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:17,559
men have it, too.

528
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:21,160
If not for today,

529
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:23,359
I wouldn't know if I'd bet right.

530
00:33:29,039 --> 00:33:30,359
My condolences, Brother Zhu.

531
00:33:34,680 --> 00:33:37,279
With you here, it's a celebratory funeral.

532
00:33:37,839 --> 00:33:38,319
Let's go.

533
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:39,160
Let's go.

534
00:33:58,559 --> 00:34:00,359
Brother Qi, come take a seat.

535
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,160
What a feast!

536
00:34:11,079 --> 00:34:12,119
Come, sit.

537
00:34:20,679 --> 00:34:21,719
People in Taiwan, China,

538
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:24,440
still keep the custom of passing away at home.

539
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:27,960
They believe dying at home makes life complete.

540
00:34:28,519 --> 00:34:29,639
Some families...

541
00:34:29,639 --> 00:34:33,119
...even pull critical elders off care to take them home.

542
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:35,760
The hospital cooperates and issues discharge papers.

543
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:37,800
Aren't people greedy?

544
00:34:38,119 --> 00:34:41,719
They want a good life and a good death to be at peace.

545
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:44,079
You are blessed.

546
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:46,119
The old lady passed away of old age.

547
00:34:46,119 --> 00:34:47,559
You and your wife didn't have to suffer.

548
00:34:47,599 --> 00:34:50,519
My blessing was waiting until you came.

549
00:34:50,960 --> 00:34:52,519
Across the strait, from top to bottom,

550
00:34:52,519 --> 00:34:54,440
there are so many people in intelligence.

551
00:34:55,039 --> 00:34:57,880
Talk all you want about courage and wits,

552
00:34:58,079 --> 00:35:00,280
there are only two and a half people I truly admire.

553
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:02,440
One is Wu Shenglai,

554
00:35:02,440 --> 00:35:03,360
and the other is you.

555
00:35:04,119 --> 00:35:05,440
Old Wu has retired now,

556
00:35:05,440 --> 00:35:06,639
so I won't get to see him.

557
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:08,280
But since you could come...

558
00:35:09,519 --> 00:35:11,400
...my life hasn't been in vain.

559
00:35:13,039 --> 00:35:15,039
I don't represent the bullshit MIB.

560
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:16,719
I'm only here for myself.

561
00:35:17,039 --> 00:35:19,000
In all sincerity, a toast to you.

562
00:35:27,239 --> 00:35:28,400
You're my senior.

563
00:35:28,639 --> 00:35:29,960
By seniority and etiquette,

564
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:31,920
I should've visited you first.

565
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:33,400
To tell you the truth,

566
00:35:33,440 --> 00:35:34,920
earning your respect

567
00:35:35,119 --> 00:35:37,280
is worth more than any golden Buddha.

568
00:35:37,559 --> 00:35:38,320
Truly.

569
00:35:39,079 --> 00:35:41,639
Besides the two of us, who's the half person?

570
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,519
It's all a haze.

571
00:35:48,199 --> 00:35:51,679
You only see a shadow, not the man.

572
00:35:53,280 --> 00:35:56,360
Mainland state security planted a mole right beside me.

573
00:35:57,199 --> 00:35:59,920
I want to know who he is, too.

574
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:02,440
Do you know?

575
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:08,559
We're all tangled up in each other.

576
00:36:09,199 --> 00:36:10,280
Zhang Fengge, Li Fengge...

577
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:11,599
The name doesn't matter.

578
00:36:11,599 --> 00:36:12,920
What matters is finding him.

579
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:14,440
You spent half your life looking and never found him.

580
00:36:14,960 --> 00:36:16,280
It'll be even harder for me.

581
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:25,599
It's been such a grueling search.

582
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:28,320
Back then, we had internal bounties.

583
00:36:28,760 --> 00:36:29,639
As long as it was anyone

584
00:36:29,639 --> 00:36:31,880
from Minzhong State Security Bureau's core staff,

585
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:33,280
a single photo and an address

586
00:36:33,280 --> 00:36:35,320
had a fixed price, paid on time.

587
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:39,639
Now the budget is drying up,

588
00:36:40,840 --> 00:36:41,719
making it even harder.

589
00:36:43,280 --> 00:36:46,239
Lin Kanshan is even more capable than Yang Shiwen.

590
00:36:46,719 --> 00:36:48,480
As long as those two legs aren't broken,

591
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:49,639
your eyes and ears

592
00:36:49,639 --> 00:36:50,960
won't go blind or deaf.

593
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:51,599
What's the rush?

594
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:53,400
The fact his legs aren't broken

595
00:36:53,519 --> 00:36:56,360
is thanks to you showing mercy, Brother Qi.

596
00:36:57,079 --> 00:36:59,320
You did far more than just aim an inch high.

597
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:01,239
If you hadn't left that yarn

598
00:37:01,239 --> 00:37:02,199
outside Lin Kanshan's door,

599
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:04,400
he would've been crippled long ago.

600
00:37:05,360 --> 00:37:06,480
Just returning a favor.

601
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:09,079
We Chinese believe in reciprocity.

602
00:37:09,199 --> 00:37:10,960
I'm not a Pixiu, hoarding without giving back.

603
00:37:15,280 --> 00:37:16,320
It was just a small token in return.

604
00:37:19,719 --> 00:37:20,599
How great is that?

605
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:25,159
You've had him by the throat ever since.

606
00:37:25,159 --> 00:37:27,400
Now he answers to you better than to me.

607
00:37:28,039 --> 00:37:30,800
Intelligence work is about making friends.

608
00:37:31,079 --> 00:37:33,400
Too bad the young folks today don't get that.

609
00:37:33,400 --> 00:37:35,440
They think intel work is just a job,

610
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:36,920
just punching the clock.

611
00:37:37,039 --> 00:37:38,639
Not a shred of human touch.

612
00:37:38,639 --> 00:37:40,039
It's getting harder and harder to lead the team.

613
00:37:40,039 --> 00:37:41,199
What can you do?

614
00:37:41,920 --> 00:37:43,719
One minute you preach pragmatism,

615
00:37:43,719 --> 00:37:45,320
the next you demand loyalty.

616
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:46,440
Of course they won't listen.

617
00:37:46,960 --> 00:37:50,480
That's why now, we talk brotherhood to outsiders,

618
00:37:50,719 --> 00:37:52,079
and enforce strict rules within.

619
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:55,280
Honestly, as long as it's valuable intel,

620
00:37:55,639 --> 00:37:58,159
it doesn't matter how you swallow it down.

621
00:37:58,239 --> 00:38:00,679
Even if it's a pile of shit, I'd eat it.

622
00:38:00,679 --> 00:38:01,800
At least it's still warm.

623
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:04,199
I hate the American way the most.

624
00:38:04,480 --> 00:38:06,400
Claiming to be so rigorous,

625
00:38:07,159 --> 00:38:08,559
with such meticulous procedures...

626
00:38:08,679 --> 00:38:10,360
In the end, results are all that matter.

627
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:16,800
Getting what you want is the only real skill.

628
00:38:17,039 --> 00:38:19,639
A general in the field must sometimes defy orders.

629
00:38:20,199 --> 00:38:21,079
Winners take all.

630
00:38:21,639 --> 00:38:23,239
Hasn't it always been like that throughout history?

631
00:38:25,199 --> 00:38:25,639
Cheers.

632
00:38:26,519 --> 00:38:27,199
However...

633
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:30,440
there must be rules.

634
00:38:30,599 --> 00:38:32,000
Those are for mediocre fools.

635
00:38:32,199 --> 00:38:35,119
True talent doesn't give a damn about that crap.

636
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:38,119
All I can say is, Brother Qi,

637
00:38:38,559 --> 00:38:41,400
if Old Zhu had been your leader back then,

638
00:38:41,599 --> 00:38:43,719
he would've worshipped you on an altar.

639
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:46,960
Disciplinary action, demotion, recall, reassignment...

640
00:38:47,159 --> 00:38:48,239
Total madness.

641
00:38:48,440 --> 00:38:49,719
Intel work is like drinking.

642
00:38:50,159 --> 00:38:51,360
If drinking with Zhang San isn't fun,

643
00:38:51,360 --> 00:38:52,800
I'll just go drink with Li Si.

644
00:38:53,119 --> 00:38:55,760
What I hate most in life is feeling suffocated.

645
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:00,199
Why do I feel like in recent years,

646
00:39:00,199 --> 00:39:01,800
your hands have been tied a bit, too?

647
00:39:03,159 --> 00:39:05,039
Times have changed.

648
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:09,639
The economic gap with Taiwan, China

649
00:39:09,639 --> 00:39:12,960
used to make turning people very easy.

650
00:39:13,159 --> 00:39:14,840
Now the mainland has reform and opening-up,

651
00:39:15,039 --> 00:39:16,519
the economy is booming,

652
00:39:16,800 --> 00:39:18,480
and getting anything done is just too hard.

653
00:39:22,440 --> 00:39:24,039
That aged wine is making me bloated.

654
00:39:24,039 --> 00:39:24,960
I'm gonna go take a leak.

655
00:39:25,079 --> 00:39:26,079
Where's the restroom?

656
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:30,840
Over here.

657
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:31,880
Okay.

658
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:44,440
Go ahead.

659
00:39:44,719 --> 00:39:45,400
Liu Shangju.

660
00:39:45,719 --> 00:39:47,079
Everyone calls her Sister Xia.

661
00:39:47,079 --> 00:39:48,760
She's Wen Zongshu's courier.

662
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,719
She just finished the polygraph test next door.

663
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:52,960
Everything was stable at first,

664
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:55,639
but before halfway through, abnormalities showed up.

665
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:57,280
She never had any issues before.

666
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:59,239
This is the first time we caught something off.

667
00:39:59,239 --> 00:40:01,000
How bad is the threat? Did you assess it?

668
00:40:01,119 --> 00:40:02,280
What's your suggestion?

669
00:40:02,280 --> 00:40:03,280
She knows everything

670
00:40:03,280 --> 00:40:04,840
about Wen Zongshu and his background.

671
00:40:05,119 --> 00:40:06,559
She was always reliable in the past.

672
00:40:06,559 --> 00:40:08,119
Something must have happened recently.

673
00:40:08,360 --> 00:40:11,199
In recent years, almost everyone got caught by the mainland.

674
00:40:11,199 --> 00:40:13,559
And the couriers are always the first to slip up.

675
00:40:13,960 --> 00:40:15,440
My suggestion is to detain her.

676
00:40:15,679 --> 00:40:17,119
What good is detaining just her?

677
00:40:17,679 --> 00:40:19,280
Didn't Wen Zongshu report anything?

678
00:40:19,280 --> 00:40:21,000
No. He probably doesn't even know.

679
00:40:21,480 --> 00:40:22,400
Got it.

680
00:40:31,599 --> 00:40:33,559
You ruined Li Fengge.

681
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:35,880
You shouldn't have done that.

682
00:40:37,679 --> 00:40:38,920
Why do I make money?

683
00:40:39,519 --> 00:40:42,559
To fund her son's wedding and build a mansion.

684
00:40:42,559 --> 00:40:45,159
Li Fengge's husband died because of me.

685
00:40:45,159 --> 00:40:47,480
I promised him I'd look after his family.

686
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:49,159
Old Zhu, oh Old Zhu...

687
00:40:49,719 --> 00:40:52,039
You completely wrecked my loyalty and honor.

688
00:40:52,039 --> 00:40:54,039
Right, right. We shouldn't have.

689
00:40:54,280 --> 00:40:56,199
The point is, you went after the wrong person.

690
00:40:56,519 --> 00:40:57,400
A total waste of effort.

691
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:59,719
What could a mere peripheral player give you?

692
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:02,679
All these years, wasn't that enough trouble for you?

693
00:41:04,039 --> 00:41:05,519
It's all dirt clods.

694
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:07,519
Put them all together,

695
00:41:07,920 --> 00:41:10,079
and they're not worth the brick you brought.

696
00:41:10,679 --> 00:41:12,320
This is a gold brick, after all.

697
00:41:16,719 --> 00:41:20,280
A stepping stone. Courtesy demands reciprocity.

698
00:41:20,840 --> 00:41:22,800
Can't let your little gold Buddha protect me for nothing.

699
00:41:29,039 --> 00:41:32,199
What's in here?

700
00:41:34,800 --> 00:41:36,480
761, 762.

701
00:41:36,480 --> 00:41:38,000
Cao Liaoping, Jia Chunlin.

702
00:41:38,840 --> 00:41:40,679
The pawns you've pushed for so many years,

703
00:41:40,679 --> 00:41:42,119
every gain and territory is right inside.

704
00:41:50,639 --> 00:41:54,159
I still want to take the rook and strike.

705
00:41:54,679 --> 00:41:57,079
I want a steady stream of intel in the future.

706
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:59,119
That's easily served up.

707
00:41:59,119 --> 00:42:00,840
As long as your appetite is big enough, brother.

708
00:42:01,039 --> 00:42:03,840
Frankly, I'll sell intelligence to the whole world.

709
00:42:03,840 --> 00:42:04,920
Not just to you.

710
00:42:08,599 --> 00:42:10,800
I don't care who you flirt with.

711
00:42:11,079 --> 00:42:13,960
Even if the same intel is split and rewoven,

712
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:15,880
as long as it's done cleverly enough,

713
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:17,599
making money from different countries

714
00:42:18,639 --> 00:42:19,920
proves you're brilliant.

715
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:24,599
Money is important,

716
00:42:24,800 --> 00:42:26,159
but satisfaction matters more.

717
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:28,039
This stuff is addictive.

718
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:29,639
Can't quit it.

719
00:42:30,599 --> 00:42:31,679
In time,

720
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:35,440
I might sway the cross-strait intelligence tides.

721
00:42:35,679 --> 00:42:37,400
Leak some intelligence today,

722
00:42:37,400 --> 00:42:39,800
and tomorrow mainland operations get moved up.

723
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:41,079
Want to bet?

724
00:42:43,639 --> 00:42:46,719
A lifetime of drinking, but today feels the best.

725
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:49,000
A toast...

726
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:53,559
to the king of underground intel in the Taiwan Strait.

727
00:42:55,199 --> 00:42:57,639
To taking the rook.

728
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,480
I'm Wang Kai,

729
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:11,199
inviting you to watch the drama series

730
00:43:11,199 --> 00:43:11,960
*Confrontation*.

731
00:43:12,280 --> 00:43:14,519
You must recount your trip back to Taipei

732
00:43:14,519 --> 00:43:16,000
to me in complete detail.

733
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:17,719
Not a single detail can be missed.

734
00:43:17,719 --> 00:43:18,559
I'm not afraid.

735
00:43:18,880 --> 00:43:19,800
Are you afraid?

736
00:43:19,800 --> 00:43:21,559
When state leaders inspect a province,

737
00:43:21,559 --> 00:43:22,440
who scouts ahead

738
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:23,360
and how they prepare in advance—

739
00:43:23,360 --> 00:43:24,559
I really know nothing about any of that.

740
00:43:24,559 --> 00:43:26,000
I wouldn't even know how to fabricate the details.

741
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:28,119
How can we determine which is the codebook?

742
00:43:28,119 --> 00:43:29,440
Check which books

743
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:31,599
are starkly out of character for Lin Kanshan.

744
00:43:33,800 --> 00:43:35,079
Why are you back?

745
00:43:35,079 --> 00:43:36,239
Coming to my own home,

746
00:43:36,239 --> 00:43:37,800
do I need to ask for your permission?
